cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite the paper below."
title: "Transfer-Operator Decoding of Structured Noise in Quantum Error Correction"
abstract: >-
  A channel-adaptive spectral decoder that represents the structured error channel
  by a truncated transfer operator (an inhomogeneous first-order Markov / classical
  matrix-product model on the code's defect graph) estimated from a small calibration
  sample, and selects the maximum-a-posteriori coset. The decoder is Bayes-optimal for
  the structured channel, reduces to the minimum-weight leader under i.i.d. noise, and
  reports the exact model posterior as a confidence that is calibrated by construction.
  This work is part of the "spectral-truncation operators" program.
